# profile: docs   -- Rust reference material permitted during a session.
#
# Kept separate from the `rust` profile on purpose: the registry is what
# cargo needs to build, this is what a student is allowed to read. They are
# different policy questions and toggle independently.
#
# Each entry covers its subdomains, so rust-exercises.com also admits
# www.rust-exercises.com.
doc.rust-lang.org          # std library docs, the Book, Rust by Example, Reference
rust-exercises.com
rustlings.rust-lang.org    # CNAME -> rust-lang.github.io (GitHub Pages)
play.rust-lang.org         # the "Run" buttons in the Book / Rust by Example
google.github.io           # Comprehensive Rust (mdBook on GitHub Pages)
docs.rs                    # per-crate API documentation

# play.rust-lang.org compiles same-origin (POST /execute), so the one hostname
# is enough. Its only external assets are Google Fonts, which the `cdn`
# profile already carries -- turning `cdn` off leaves it working but unstyled.

# Comprehensive Rust is one hostname because mdBook bundles its own CSS, JS and
# fonts, so every asset the book renders from is same-origin. Its "Run" buttons
# POST to play.rust-lang.org, already above. What stays blocked is cosmetic or
# unwanted: three img.shields.io badges on the landing page (broken-image icons,
# nothing else), and googletagmanager / gstatic, which are analytics and the
# cookie-consent bar.
#
# docs.rs is also one hostname: every asset a crate's documentation page needs
# is served from docs.rs itself, and there is no static. sibling to name. It
# carries the docs for every published crate, which is the point -- a student
# reading about a dependency should not have to guess from the source.
#
# google.github.io admits Google's other GitHub Pages projects too -- the entry
# matches the host and its subdomains, and per-path allowing is not something
# DNS can express. That is the whole of the widening. Being GitHub Pages, its
# edge IPs are already in static4.list, so the book survives a laptop on
# encrypted DNS this router never sees.

# Deliberately NOT included -- add with `classnet allow add <host> docs` if wanted:
#   asciinema.org       the demo recording on the rustlings landing page.
#   www.rust-lang.org   nav links out of both sites.
#   plausible.io        analytics on rust-exercises.com; nothing renders from it.
